@startuml UC007_Save_Collaborators_Sequence
!theme plain
title UC007 — Save project collaborators

actor "Creator or another owner" as Editor
participant "public/js/app.js" as App
participant "public/js/api.js" as Client
participant "src/routes/project.routes.js" as API
participant "src/middleware/requireAuth.js" as Auth
participant "src/services/projectService.js" as Service
participant "src/domain/projectRules.js" as Rules
participant "src/db/database.js" as Data
database PostgreSQL as DB

note over App, API
  Collaborators are saved in the existing project request.
  UC002 uses POST /api/projects.
  UC003 uses PUT /api/projects/:id with If-Match.
end note

Editor -> App : Enter a teammate’s Folio email
App -> Client : Look up the exact email
Client -> API : POST /api/projects/collaborators/lookup
API -> Auth : Verify active session
Auth --> API : Identify editor
API -> Data : Look up the Folio account
Data --> API : Name, email, and public showroom ID
API --> Client : Matching account
Client --> App : Display name and email for selection

Editor -> App : Select Folio accounts and roles,\nadd optional notes, and click Save changes
App -> Client : Submit project data and collaboration fields
Client -> API : Send authenticated multipart project request
API -> Auth : Verify active session
Auth --> API : Identify editor
API -> Service : Create or update the project
Service -> Rules : Validate collaborator entries and notes
Rules --> Service : Validated collaboration data
Service -> Data : Save project and collaboration changes
Data -> DB : Resolve accounts and check membership and revision on edit
Data -> DB : Save project, notes, and memberships in one transaction
DB --> Data : Commit project and collaborators
Data --> Service : Saved project
Service --> API : Project with updated collaborators
API --> Client : Saved project response and ETag
Client --> App : Refresh saved project
App --> Editor : Display updated collaboration settings

note over Data, DB
  Published projects appear in each current collaborator’s showroom.
end note

@enduml
